<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-module-holocaust-museum-visit" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Zekelman Holocaust Center Module</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>This module is intended to be completed while visiting the Zekelman Holocaust Center.</p>
  </introduction>

  <section xml:id="sec-module-holocaust-museum-visit-norms">
    <title>Discussion Norms</title>
<p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <p>Take care of your well-being and step out if needed</p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Share the air</p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>Monitor how much you're participating/how much space you're occupying</p></li>
          <li><p>Avoid interrupting folks</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Seek first to understand, then to be understood</p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>Revoice what folks say or ask for clarifying questions before responding</p></li>
          <li><p>Practice active listening</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Speak for yourself, not others</p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>Avoid generalizations</p></li>
          <li><p>Respect others' experiences</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Consider whose viewpoints are being excluded</p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Use both/and rather than either/or thinking</p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>“Yes, and” language</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Be aware of, and work to deconstruct, the existing power dynamics in the room</p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Presume positive intentions</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</p>


  </section>

  <section xml:id="sec-module-intro-prompts">
    <title>Introduction and Reflection</title>
    <p>
  In your groups, discuss the following:
  <ol>
    <li>
      <p>Share your names and introduce yourselves to one another.</p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Take 5 minutes to write down your thoughts reflecting on the tour. Think about:</p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>What stuck out to you?</p></li>
          <li><p>What do you think will stay with you?</p></li>
          <li><p>How has it shaped your understanding of the work your individual/organization did?</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Now take ~10 minutes to share out some of your reflections with your peers (just 1-2 minutes per student).</p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>Share the individual or organization you are studying:</p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>Why you chose that individual/organization</p></li>
          <li><p>What you have found so far</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>
    
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sec-module-ethical-codes">
    <title>Modern Professional Ethical Codes</title>
    <p>Now we will turn to ethics. Your individual or organization's contributions were in some area of STEM and today, 
    STEM professionals are bound by ethical guidelines and codes. Review the appropriate guidelines for the STEM area you have chosen.</p>
    <p>
    <ol>
      <li>
      <p>Actuarial Science</p>
        <p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.soa.org/4934e8/globalassets/assets/files/static-pages/about/governance/soa-code-of-professional-conduct.pdf" visual="www.soa.org/4934e8/globalassets/assets/files/static-pages/about/governance/soa-code-of-professional-conduct.pdf">SOA Code of Professional Conduct</url>
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.casact.org/about/professionalism/code-professional-conduct " visual="https://www.casact.org/about/professionalism/code-professional-conduct ">Casualty Actuarial Society Code of Professional Conduct</url>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>

        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
      <p>Biology, Pharmacology, and Health</p>
        <p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/chapters" visual="https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/chapters">American Medical Association Code of Medical Ethics (by Chapter)</url>
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.pharmacist.com/Code-of-Ethics" visual="https://www.pharmacist.com/Code-of-Ethics">American Pharmacists Association Code of Ethics for Pharmacists</url>
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.apa.org/ethics/code  " visual="https://www.apa.org/ethics/code">American Psychological Association Ethical Principles of Psychologists and Code of Conduct</url>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>

      </p>
      </li>
      <li>
      <p>Chemistry</p>
        <p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.acs.org/careers/career-services/ethics/the-chemical-professionals-code-of-conduct.html " visual="https://www.acs.org/careers/career-services/ethics/the-chemical-professionals-code-of-conduct.html ">American Chemical Society Chemical Professional's Code of Conduct (intended for domestic US members)</url>
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.acs.org/content/dam/acsorg/global/international/scifreedom/global-chemists-code-of-ethics-fi-2016.pdf " visual="https://www.acs.org/content/dam/acsorg/global/international/scifreedom/global-chemists-code-of-ethics-fi-2016.pdf ">American Chemical Society Global Chemist's Code of Ethics (intended for international members)</url>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>

      </p>
      </li>
      <li>
      <p>Computer Science</p>
        <p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.acm.org/code-of-ethics" visual="https://www.acm.org/code-of-ethics">Association for Computing Machinery Code of Ethics</url>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>

      </p>
      </li>
      <li>
      <p>Engineering</p>
        <p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.asce.org/career-growth/ethics/code-of-ethics " visual="https://www.asce.org/career-growth/ethics/code-of-ethics ">American Society of Civil Engineers Code of Ethics</url>
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.asme.org/getmedia/1d9d64bf-f6a7-4e75-a8f5-0cabd8c04269/p-15-7-ethics_2.pdf " visual="https://www.asme.org/getmedia/1d9d64bf-f6a7-4e75-a8f5-0cabd8c04269/p-15-7-ethics_2.pdf ">American Society of Mechanical Engineers Code of Ethics</url>
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.nspe.org/career-growth/nspe-code-ethics-engineers " visual="https://www.nspe.org/career-growth/nspe-code-ethics-engineers ">National Society of Professional Engineers Code of Ethics for Engineers</url>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
      </p>
      </li>
      <li>
      <p>Statistics</p>
        <p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p><url href="https://www.amstat.org/your-career/ethical-guidelines-for-statistical-practice " visual="https://www.amstat.org/your-career/ethical-guidelines-for-statistical-practice ">American Statistical Association Ethical Guidelines for Statistical Practice</url>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
      </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    </p> 
</section>

<section xml:id="sec-module-ethical-codes-discussion">
  <title>Ethical Codes Discussion</title>
    <p>
  In your groups, discuss the following:
  <ol>
    <li>
      <p>What guidelines did your individual or organization violate?</p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>Were the activities a clear violation or do they depend on some interpretation?</p></li>
          <li><p>When were the guidelines established in history?</p></li>
          <li><p>Consider that these guidelines are updated regularly - how far back do the guidelines go?</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>How are the ethical guidelines you identified enforced? </p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>What responsibilities (if any) do others in the profession have to report one who violates the ethical guidelines?</p></li>
          <li><p>Is there a formal governing body that oversees their enforcement? How is it structured?</p></li>
          <li><p>What are the consequences of violating the ethical guidelines?</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>
      <li>
      <p>What language (if any) is there that suggests how the governing body in your profession views what it means to be an ethical scientist? </p>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>Do the ethical guidelines suggest an affirmative duty to good or merely an obligation to not do harm?</p></li>
          <li><p>Do you agree with that perspective? Why or why not?</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>

</section>

<section xml:id="sec-module-ethical-lenses-discussion">
  <title>Framework for Ethical Decision Making</title>
  <p>The Santa Clara Markkula Center for Applied Ethics has a website describing a <url href="https://www.scu.edu/ethics/ethics-resources/a-framework-for-ethical-decision-making/" visual="https://www.scu.edu/ethics/ethics-resources/a-framework-for-ethical-decision-making/">Framework for Ethical Decision Making</url>.</p>
  <p> This includes a list of five ethical lenses. An ethical lens is how one thinks about and applies ethics in their decisions. Read through the list of lenses and discuss the following with your group (make sure to record your answers!):</p>
  <p>
  <ul>
    <li> Which len(es) do you identify strongest with? Why? </li> 
    <li> Which len(es) do you think embody the ethical guidelines you reviewed? Justify your answers.</li> 
  </ul>
  </p>

</section>


<section xml:id="sec-module-stem-professional-discussion">
  <title>STEM Professionals</title>
  <p>Science is powerful. Having studied how a STEM professional contributed to the Holocaust and viewed artifacts documenting the history of the Holocaust, you have seen some of the worst ways to use that power.  </p>
  <p>Having reviewed ethical guidelines for a STEM profession, you have seen current minimal expectations for how to use that power responsibly.</p>
  <p> Take some time to think, and then write down, what you think being an Ethical STEM professional means to you and what this will look like for your conduct in the workplace. </p>
  <p>Here are some prompts to get you started, but feel free to deviate from this list: </p>
  <p>
  <ul>
    <li> What have you learned about ethical guidelines in your profession and your perspective on ethical professional practice? </li> 
    <li> How did the tour of the Holocaust Center and your examination of the scientific contributions to the Holocaust illustrate the need for science ethics? How does that shape your view of ethical science practice?</li> 
  </ul>
  </p>

</section>

</chapter>